insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('93f7e269-392d-5072-bd4b-5deb3fc38102', 'rg3-argument-evidence-p06', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g3-argument-evidence'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Penguins and Puffins$q$, $q$Penguins and puffins are both black and white sea birds. At first glance, they look a lot alike. If you look closely, though, you will find many differences.

Both birds are excellent swimmers. They use their wings to push through the water as they chase fish. Both have thick feathers that keep them warm and dry in cold seas.

The biggest difference is in the air. Puffins can fly. They flap their small wings very fast and zoom over the waves. Penguins, however, cannot fly at all. Their wings are stiff and shaped like flippers. Because their wings work like paddles, penguins are faster swimmers than puffins.

The two birds also live in different places. Most penguins live in the southern half of the world. Puffins live in the northern half. So the two birds almost never meet in the wild.

Their beaks are different, too. A puffin has a bright orange and yellow beak in spring. A penguin's beak stays the same color all year.$q$, 'draft')
