-- Passage rg3-authors-purpose-p05
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('2a906249-aa56-518e-a31e-aa2d46c45d63', 'rg3-authors-purpose-p05', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g3-authors-purpose'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Why Every Kid Should Play Music$q$, $q$Every child should learn to play a musical instrument. It might be a drum, a violin or a simple recorder. Any instrument is a great place to start.

Playing music teaches patience. When I started piano lessons, my fingers felt stiff and slow. I practiced a little every day. After a few months, I could play a whole song. Learning an instrument shows kids that hard work pays off.

Music also brings people together. In a school band, every player has a part. The song only sounds right when everyone listens and plays as a team.

Best of all, music is fun. Playing a happy tune can cheer you up on a gloomy day. You can play for your family, your friends or just yourself.

Some kids worry that they are not good at music. But nobody is good at the start. Ask your teacher or family to help you try an instrument this year. You might discover a new favorite thing.$q$, 'draft')
